From: adb-rt (armv7-pc-windows-msvc port)
Subject: [PATCH] libusb 1.0.28: backport upstream's Windows hotplug backend

*** VENDORED FROM UPSTREAM libusb, NOT WRITTEN HERE. ***

Upstream commit:  5b870b633e0720e51218908c7b369d877cb253e6
                  2026-07-02, Sylvain Fasel <sylvain@sonatique.net>
                  "windows: register hotplug window class with this copy's module handle"
Source:           https://github.com/libusb/libusb

WHY
  adb's libusb backend cannot start on Windows with a stock libusb release, on ANY
  architecture. client/usb_libusb.cpp:1064 calls libusb_hotplug_register_callback and
  LOG(FATAL)s at :1072 if it fails -- which aborts the adb server process.

    hotplug.c:361          returns LIBUSB_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED without the capability
    core.c:2655            capability is !(usbi_backend.get_device_list)
    windows_common.c:891   the Windows backend defines get_device_list unconditionally
    ChangeLog:191          "Add hotplug support for Darwin and Linux"  -- never Windows

  This is also why AOSP hardcodes is_libusb_enabled() = false on _WIN32
  (client/transport_usb.cpp:182-184): the backend cannot work there.

  Upstream solved it behind the LIBUSB_WINDOWS_HOTPLUG build option. This backports that
  one feature into the pinned 1.0.28 release rather than moving to master, which would
  drag every other change since 1.0.28 onto an untested platform.

WHAT IS IN HERE
  new   libusb/os/windows_hotplug.c   verbatim from the commit above (431 lines)
  new   libusb/os/windows_hotplug.h   verbatim from the commit above
  edit  libusb/libusbi.h              declare usbi_attach_device / usbi_detach_device
  edit  libusb/core.c                 split connect/disconnect into attach/detach + notify,
                                      exactly as the commit does. Behaviour-preserving:
                                      the existing bodies are unchanged, only factored.
  edit  libusb/os/windows_common.h    +2 fields on winusb_device_priv (seen_during_scan,
                                      seen_before_scan), verbatim from the commit
  edit  libusb/os/windows_common.c    the 5 LIBUSB_WINDOWS_HOTPLUG hooks
  edit  libusb/os/windows_winusb.c    5 hunks so enumeration attaches devices itself

WHY windows_winusb.c HAD TO CHANGE
  1.0.28's usbi_alloc_device() attaches a device to the context only when
  !libusb_has_capability(LIBUSB_CAP_HAS_HOTPLUG) (core.c:725). Once the capability is 1 the
  CORE stops attaching and the BACKEND must do it. Without these hunks the build reports
  HAS_HOTPLUG=1 and enumerates ZERO devices -- it would pass a naive gate and never see a
  phone.

NOT TAKEN, DELIBERATELY
  Master's windows_winusb.c also carries an unrelated interface_lock/initialized concurrency
  refactor (29 of its 38 diff hunks). Taking the file wholesale fails to build against
  1.0.28: it needs a libusb_device_string_type enum in the PUBLIC libusb.h and a new
  get_device_string slot in usbi_os_backend, which shifts every later function pointer and
  breaks every other backend. That is "move libusb to master", which this port does not do.
  Only the hotplug hunks are taken.

VERIFIED
  x64 usbprobe on the dev box:
    LIBUSB_CAP_HAS_HOTPLUG           -> 1
    libusb_get_device_list           -> 13 device(s)
    libusb_hotplug_register_callback -> 0 (OK)
  ARM32: builds clean, 13/13 objects ARMNT. NOT RUN -- needs device.
